Subject: [PATCH 1/2] aiter: retune the M=64 decode a16w16 GEMMs for Llama-3.1-8B on gfx950

REJECTED -- DO NOT APPLY. Measured end-to-end regression. Kept as a recorded negative
result; see FINDINGS.md #4.

MEASUREMENT
  Isolated, graph-captured, LLC-overflowing working set (analysis/race_gemm_candidates.py
  --m 64 --footprint-mb 1024), vs what the stack resolves today:
    o_proj   (4096, 4096)   flydsl:3511  13.932 us -> hipblaslt:438482  12.859 us  +7.70%
    down_proj(4096,14336)   torch        28.973 us -> hipblaslt:440151  27.654 us  +4.55%
    qkv_proj (6144, 4096)   flydsl:2331  16.170 us -> hipblaslt:438484  15.823 us  +2.15%
    gate_up  (28672,4096)   torch        43.506 us -> no candidate beat the fallback
  = 2.74 us of 102.6 us of GEMM per layer-step, and GEMM is 20.16% of decode.

  End-to-end, 6 paired restart-to-restart rounds with the arm order flipped every round
  (analysis/ab_campaign.sh), bench/ against a bench/ baseline:
    base 2638.411 tok/s   cand 2628.008 tok/s   -0.394% +/- 0.066% (2*SEM)
    mean TPOT  20.372 ms -> 20.478 ms  (+0.52%)   <-- this patch's term
    mean TTFT 3986.2  ms -> 3978.6  ms (-0.19%)   <-- patch 2/2's term
  All six paired deltas negative, sd 0.055%. The kernels are faster in isolation and
  slower in the server. Reverting is the result.

APPLY
  cd /sgl-workspace/aiter && patch -p1 < <this file>
  rm -rf /tmp/aiter_configs      # merged table is regenerated only when absent
  # then restart the server: the GEMM table is consumed at HIP-graph capture time
  # revert: python3 analysis/deploy_gemm_rows.py revert   (restores from analysis/gemm_tune/base/)

BASE
  aiter d9e5ef7ce08ee7045d583aed768cff41aa9210fe; recorded copies of the two edited files
  are in analysis/gemm_tune/base/.

WHY THESE TWO FILES ARE EDITED IN PLACE
  Llama-3.1-8B has no tuned-GEMM config of its own. It inherits (64,4096,4096) from
  qwen3_5_397b_bf16_tuned_gemm.csv and (64,6144,4096) from glm5_bf16_tuned_gemm.csv,
  because those models happen to share the shape. Shipping the same keys in a new
  model_configs file makes aiter/jit/core.py:295 raise on the duplicate and auto-resolve
  by the `us` column -- the tuner's eager `us`, which is exactly the metric shown to
  mis-rank these kernels. So the rows must be replaced where they live, which also changes
  those two shapes for GLM/Qwen on this GPU. Only (64,4096,14336) is a genuinely new key
  and goes in the new file.

  The `us` values written here are the graph-measured numbers above, not the tuner's.

NOTE
  The flydsl row replaced for o_proj carried err_ratio 0.0198; the hipblaslt row is exact.
  See FINDINGS.md #6 -- that accuracy difference was gated and is not visible in gsm8k.

